  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-25: "Continue with next tasks". Issue #2457 (read it in full: gh issue view 2457 --comments). `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/AssignTaskRecipientGate.cs` (task 168, PR #2418; task 207 added AdministrativeAccount) copies "which internal user represents this contact" from `Api/ExternalAccess/GrantAccessNotifier.cs` because uac-r2's shared `ContactUserRepresentation` was not on master. It now is: `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/ExternalAccess/ContactUserRepresentation.cs`. uac-r2's guidance (in the issue): call `ContactUserRepresentation.ResolveAsync` with `BindingColumnMissingPolicy.DecideOnLink`; its per-user `ClassifyEligibility` takes `rootIsRestricted` directly, so read the Restricted flag once up front; keep the gate's two intended differences from the notifier (D-199): `SeveralUsers` refuses (no email), and eligibility is applied after the count.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF (Signals, ExternalAccess).</role>
  <goal>The gate decides who represents the assignee contact through ContactUserRepresentation, with exactly the same email/no-email outcome and warning code as today for every input, and no copied representation logic remains in the gate.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>This is a reuse swap, not a behaviour change. Before editing: fetch master; read ContactUserRepresentation, GrantAccessNotifier (its caller) and the gate; list each branch of the gate's copied logic and the matching ContactUserRepresentation outcome in notes/task-215-notes.md; any input where they would disagree is an escalation, not a silent change. Task 207's AdministrativeAccount refinement and the rights-answer decider stay. uac-r2 owns ContactUserRepresentation: do not edit it; if it lacks something the gate needs, STOP and report. Run the gate and notifier tests unmodified first as the behaviour baseline.</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha 2026-11-24">Run the relevant --filter (for Signals code "FullyQualifiedName~Signals", which includes contract baselines; for Communication code "FullyQualifiedName~Communication"); update any baseline the change moves in the same PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene: publish-size delta vs fresh master (short paths, same zip tool, file counts) in the PR; no new HIGH CVE; no new package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11">No new service, interface or DI registration unless the three questions are answered in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6">Filtered BFF tests only (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); full ArchTests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="public repo">No environment GUIDs, user or contact ids, mailbox addresses or tenant names in code, tests, notes or the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Security fails closed; two independent review passes (auth tag).</constraint>
